PRE-REGISTRATION -- multi-query non-inferiority run              2026-09-12
Written BEFORE the run. Fixes the design error the third addendum named in
itself: the previous runs used a SUPERIORITY test, and failing to reject is
not evidence of equivalence.

WHY THE PREVIOUS RUN COULD NOT SETTLE THIS, AND WHY REPEATING IT WON'T
  n=142 was the WHOLE catalogue -- the population is exhausted, and measurement
  noise is zero (two invocations returned byte-identical scores), so neither a
  larger sample nor more repetitions exists to be had. FULL vs FIRST produced
  only 15 discordant pairs (11-4, p=0.1185) because each skill contributes a
  single 0/1 outcome, and 127 of 142 skills flipped the same way in both arms
  and carried no information at all.
  The available axis is QUERIES PER SKILL, not skills. 140 skills have >=4
  usable body paragraphs, so 3 queries each = 420 queries per arm. Each skill
  then contributes a GRADED 0-3 score per arm, and a skill where FIRST scores
  2/3 against FULL's 3/3 becomes evidence instead of a tie.

CLUSTERING -- the analysis must respect it
  Three queries drawn from ONE skill are NOT independent observations. Treating
  420 queries as 420 independent trials would inflate significance. The unit of
  analysis is therefore the SKILL: per arm, score each skill 0-3; the paired
  comparison runs over the 140 skill-level differences, never over raw queries.

PRIMARY -- non-inferiority of FIRST against FULL
  MARGIN: 5 percentage points, fixed here, before data. Justification stated in
  advance so it cannot be tuned afterwards: FIRST saves 15,038 tokens per
  iteration (46% of a 32,768 window, 11.5% of the deployed 131,072). A loss of
  up to 5pp of skill-selection accuracy is worth that saving; a loss beyond 5pp
  is not.
  TEST: one-sided 95% upper confidence bound on (FULL - FIRST) over skill-level
  mean scores, via the paired bootstrap over SKILLS (resample skills, not
  queries -- that is what preserves the clustering).
    upper bound <  5pp -> NON-INFERIOR. The 66% saving is safe to build, and
                          the addendum's "cannot exclude a 10pp loss" caveat is
                          discharged and must be updated in place.
    upper bound >= 5pp -> NOT DEMONSTRATED. The recommendation stays unproven;
                          say so and do not ship the shortened catalogue on the
                          strength of this ADR.
  Note both outcomes are reportable and neither is a failure. "Not demonstrated"
  is the honest result if the interval stays wide.

SECONDARY -- NAMES against FULL, same machinery
  Expected to reconfirm decisively. NAMES is NOT a non-inferiority candidate;
  it is reported as a superiority comparison for continuity with the n=142 run.

CONTROL -- FULL remains the positive control
  VOID below 25%, as in the full-catalogue run, and for the same reason: a
  boundary placed at the observed value is satisfiable by stasis (guard-5645).
  Empty completions abort as INSTRUMENT failures, never score as wrong answers
  (guard-6562).

WHAT WILL NOT BE DONE
  The margin will not be moved after seeing the interval. Exact match stays the
  metric. Queries are drawn by the SAME rule as before (body paragraphs, front
  matter and headings and code spans stripped) -- only the COUNT per skill
  changes, so the previous runs remain comparable.
